    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup for July 25th is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns a standout 81.88 efficiency score against Bryce Elder. **Henderson**\u2019s massive advantage is fueled by an optimal #3 spot and a favorable dynamic platoon split against the right-handed Elder, making him the cornerstone of today\u2019s offensive strategy. **Drake Baldwin** also emerges as a high-upside play at 71.83; while we are waiting on official lineup confirmation, his projected leadoff duties combined with a +16% park factor and high xwOBA metrics against Brandon Young suggest a multi-run performance is well within reach. **Sam Antonacci** (67.67) and **Heliot Ramos** (66.52) round out our top-tier tier, with the latter benefiting specifically from wind-out conditions and an elevated #2 order slot that maximizes his exposure against R. Johnson.\n\nIn the mid-tier, we are leaning into volume and speed, particularly with **Jackson Merrill** (60.12). Despite a tougher matchup against Eu. P\u00e9rez, **Merrill** is a vital start due to his 88% success rate on the basepaths, providing the scarcity value we require in a 5x5 Roto environment. The tightest decision today was the exclusion of **Curtis Mead** (55.76) from the active roster. While **Mead** is in a solid spot against Bratt, he ultimately couldn't eclipse the efficiency scores of **Miguel Vargas** (60.61) or **Jacob Wilson** (59.54), as the optimizer prioritized **Vargas**\u2019s superior xwOBA and **Wilson**\u2019s likely leadoff placement. \n\nRisks remain, as nearly every player in our lineup is currently marked \"Lineup Pending.\" We are proceeding with the assumption that **Drake Baldwin**, **Coby Mayo**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Dominic Smith** will occupy the slots reflected in these projections. Furthermore, note that **Kyle Tucker** carries a lower score of 51.42; he is currently our most risky asset today due to facing the high-caliber arm of Nolan McLean and a -14% SP skill handicap, but he remains in the lineup as a hedge against his elite ceiling. Monitor the weather and late lineup changes for **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Jung**, **Wade Meckler**, **Luis Lara**, and **Cole Carrigg** to ensure our bench depth is optimized should a late-inning replacement be required.",
